COROSYNC FLOW-CONTROL BUG -- DLF runs 2 and 3 (non-master ingress; both directions at once)
===========================================================================
Run:    2026-09-25 11:32-11:38 NZST (device clock 23:32-23:38 UTC 09-24), tb470
Build:  awplus_main-20260923-20 (stack and IE520-sa)
DUT:    IE520 3-member VCStack "IE520-stk", members 1/3/4, member 3 = Active Master, all
        Ready, Normal operation. Static LAG sa3 (stack port1.0.13 + port4.0.9 <-> IE520-sa
        port1.0.13 + port1.0.9) carries eth2's traffic INTO the stack on members 1 and 4.
Bug:    see warmup-run1.log (corosync "Enabling/Disabling flow control" log storm with
        `terminal monitor` on while DLF crosses the stack link).

VERDICT: NOT REPRODUCED. Line-rate DLF into the non-master members (run 2), and line-rate
         DLF into the master AND the non-master members at the same time (run 3), were
         flooded in hardware with the expected egress behaviour, the CPUs saw ~1,000
         packets per window, and the stack logged NOTHING: no corosync line, no "flow
         control" line, one dhclient Solicit on the console in six minutes.

SETUP (as run 1; sender frames 1496 B built = 1500 on the wire, dst 02:00:00:00:99:99,
       UDP 5010 -> 10, never learned -- MAC gate confirmed absent before the runs)
  tb eth2 (00f0.4d00.7717) -> IE520-sa port1.0.2 -> sa3 -> stack members 1 + 4   sender 2
  tb eth3 (00f0.4d00.7718) -> master port3.0.9                                    sender 3
  tb eth1 (00f0.4d00.7716) -> master port3.0.13                                   receiver
  tcpreplay --topspeed --loop=0 --duration=10 per sender; tcpdump -w /dev/null per
  (receiver, sender) pair filtered on the sender's MAC + UDP sport 5010; kernel drops 0.

RUN 2 -- DLF from eth2 only (ingress IE520-sa, enters the stack on members 1/4 via sa3)
  window 11:34:24-11:34:34   sent eth2 822,501 @ 984.2 Mbps, 82,234 pps
  rx eth1 <- eth2  822,501 (100%)      rx eth3 <- eth2  822,501 (100%)
  CPU rx per member (sdma rxDmaPcktCnt, clear-on-read; before-run values are the
