  sent; console left at the exec prompt.

NOTES
  - Two senders at once: tcpreplay on eth3 fell to 957 Mbps while eth2 held 984 -- the
    host, not the DUT (the same NIC did 984 alone in run 1).
  - Together with run 1 this covers: DLF into the master, into the non-master members, and
    into both simultaneously, each at 1G line rate with 1500-byte frames, for 10 s. On this
    build the corosync symptom did not appear. What this bench cannot do: 10G ingress, or a
    DIRECT NIC on member 1 (eth2's path enters via the SA and the LAG). Terrence's planned
    recable (an eth port from u5 to member 1, replacing the x230 link) gives the direct
    member-1 ingress; repeat run 3 after it.
  - Method file: the drivers (tdlf1.py, tdlf2.py) live in the session scratchpad; recipe =
    scapy-built pcap of 500 identical 1496-B frames, tcpreplay --topspeed, tcpdump counting
    with -s 64 -B 65536, sdma read before/after, `terminal monitor` on the master console
    read by a thread that logs each line as it arrives.
